# held/civil/staff_run: the staff (art weapon 4) carried in the run facing right, in the near (right) hand (PROPS, P2b
# fix B10-CIVIL-STAFF-RUN-ATLAS; staff_runl.pxm the same facing left).
# The run swings the hand from behind the hip (runB) past it (N) to high in front (runF); staff.pxm's rest view, fixed to
# the grip, swept its head out in front of the face with the swing and widened the run's frames past B10's 64 KB. Keyed
# on the arm and drawn only in the RUN part (`when run replace` over empty bases: the arm keys are the walk's and the
# hurt's too), so each swing has its own carry: behind the hip and at it the staff leans back over the near shoulder in
# front of the head (layer held, the fingers over the shaft: regions H), its head over the back of the hair; high in
# front it stands upright behind the head (layer neck), its head clear over the crown. staff.pxm hands the side views
# over in the run (its R and L rest views `when run` draw nothing). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# PROTO6 i3 (2026-10-22; the run's lean 4 and the wider arm pump): pB carries the staff upright at the hand (no lean back), pF
# grips it 3 rows higher up the shaft (the woman's 3), pM stands it behind the head (layer neck: it no longer crosses the face),
# pK upright: the robed scholars' RUN atlases stay in B10's 64 KB.
use person
body man woman
role held staff
layer neck
anchor grip
keys armR
z 40

view D key runB origin 0 0
|.

view D key N origin 0 0
|.

view D key runF origin 0 0
|.

view U key runB origin 0 0
|.

view U key N origin 0 0
|.

view U key runF origin 0 0
|.

view R key runB origin 0 0
|.

view R key N origin 0 0
|.

view R key runF origin 0 0
|.

view L key runB origin 0 0
|.

view L key N origin 0 0
|.

view L key runF origin 0 0
|.

